# Git workflow (project-ffb3)

Applies to all future work on this project. Do not retroactively reorganize past work.

## Commits and GitHub

After each logical change (feature slice, fix, or wiring step):

1. Commit on the current feature branch with a clear message focused on **why**.
2. Push to GitHub (`git push -u origin <branch>` on first push for that branch).
3. Do not leave completed work only in the working tree — if code was written or changed, commit and push it before moving on.

Ask before force-push, amend after push, or other destructive git operations.

## Feature branches

Use one branch per major project area. Create or switch to the appropriate branch before starting work in that area.

| Area | Branch (example) |
|------|------------------|
| PAB / tier valuation | `pab-valuation` |
| Career projection | `career-projection` |
| Draft pick value | `draft-value` |
| Data import / schema | `data-pipeline` |
| UI / players pages | `player-ui` |

Branch names: lowercase kebab-case, scoped to the feature. If work spans areas, pick the primary branch or split into focused PRs per branch.

## Workflow per task

1. Confirm or create the feature branch for the section being worked on.
2. Implement the change.
3. Commit + push.
4. Open or update a PR when a section milestone is ready (use `gh pr create` when asked).

## What not to do

- Do not batch many unrelated sections into one branch.
- Do not retroactively create branches or commits for work already done before this rule.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials).
